Murphy, 41, a West Brighton resident, also alluded to Grimm's defense of GOP presidential candidate Mitt Romney's "I like to fire people" comment.
"My opponent might like to fire people," he said. "I like hiring people and I want to put America back to work now."
Grimm (R-Staten Island/Brooklyn) and the GOP House majority in December voted against a measure that would have extended tax cuts and unemployment benefits for two months, but in the face of a public firestorm, they quickly backpedaled and approved the measure.
