Suffolk County Executive Steve Bellone, who often stresses the need for long-term vision, said Wednesday his second term will let him start implementing his blueprint for rebuilding Suffolk's downtowns and creating new rapid bus lanes to ease transit, and sewer lines to protect water resources.
"The first term was all about getting the county out of crisis," Bellone said. "The second term is all about creating a better future, and economic development is crucial for that."
Bellone, a Democrat, made his comments a day after scoring a 25,000-vote victory Tuesday over Republican James O'Connor.
Sounding conciliatory on election night, Bellone called on the six-member Republican legislative caucus to "work together" with Democrats to create "a bright future for all of us in this county. It's time for us to come together to do the peoples' business."
